WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.200
- Are you someone who's
crazy about Christmas?

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.950
- I love Christmas, I get--

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.783
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.783 --> 00:00:05.616
Yeah!

00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:06.861
(crowd cheering)

00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:09.950
- Did you have a favorite
present, growing up?

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.920
Like for Christmas?

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.820
I have one.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.760
- Oh, you do?

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.370
- My first song I ever
wrote on was my key--

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.000
We didn't have any money
and my mom pulled together,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.370
totally on credit,

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.780
and got me a keyboard.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:20.680
- That's nice.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.560
I think that my family
did give me a little

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.500
sing-along microphone thing,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.527
but then they were like,

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:29.364
"Forget that, that's not gonna work out."

00:00:29.364 --> 00:00:32.400
Every year I wanted baby dolls.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.030
I really always wanted a baby doll,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.590
and then one year the
hot, cool doll of the year

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.540
was this baby called Baby Feels So Real.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.900
And you would touch the baby

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.420
and would have bones and stuff in it!

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.420
Do you guys remember this?

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.170
I don't know why I remember that doll,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.250
'cause that's creepy.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.304
- That's...

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:55.500
My daughter ha--

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.587
- Who was like, "We should make a doll,

00:00:57.587 --> 00:00:59.580
"and put bones in it."

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.413
- Yeah

00:01:00.413 --> 00:01:01.300
- "and give it to children."

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.640
- My daughter has a creepy doll.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.000
She has a creepy doll that she loves,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.800
and I'm always trying to misplace it...

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.023
- Let's put that away.

00:01:09.023 --> 00:01:09.911
- And she's like, "Where's my doll?"

00:01:09.911 --> 00:01:10.744
- Yeah, and you're like, "No."

00:01:10.744 --> 00:01:11.577
- It's super creepy,

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:13.840
it looks like it's from
a haunted horror movie,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.673
kinda thing.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.506
But that's okay.

00:01:15.506 --> 00:01:16.339
- Yeah, I had a lot of those,

00:01:16.339 --> 00:01:17.210
I had a doll too

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.470
where you had to teach it to learn words.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.630
So I'd be like, "It's apple."

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:23.540
Or like, "Spaghetti."

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.050
And it'd be like, "Asghetti."

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:25.883
And I'd be like, "No! It's spaghetti!"

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:27.683
Like over and over.

00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:28.516
- You'd argue?

00:01:28.516 --> 00:01:31.100
- And then they'd get it right

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.544
and I was like, "I just
taught that doll a word."

00:01:33.544 --> 00:01:36.037
- "I'm gonna be a great mom."

